# Boxy — Cursor Project Intelligence

## What Is This Project?

Boxy is a multi-tenant event streaming library built directly on top of a relational database
(MySQL 8.0+, PostgreSQL in progress). It provides Apache Pulsar-like semantics — topics,
partitions, subscriptions, consumer groups, cursor commits — over a transactional outbox.
No broker process, no Kafka, no Pulsar.

**The authoritative client protocol is four stored procedures:**
- `sp_consumers__register` — register a consumer instance
- `sp_events__poll` — poll for events (returns events + polling probability)
- `sp_cursors__commit` — commit cursor positions
- `sp_consumers__deregister` — deregister a consumer

Any language can implement a Boxy client. The Java module (`boxy-core`) is a reference
implementation, not the authoritative one.

---

## Critical Patterns — Do This

### Stored Procedures
- Every write procedure MUST have an EXIT HANDLER FOR SQLEXCEPTION with ROLLBACK + RESIGNAL
- Filename MUST match procedure name exactly: `sp_consumers__register.sql`
- Double underscore between entity and action: `sp_<entity>__<action>`
- Comment every parameter, return value, and error code at the top of the file
- Use MEMORY tables for temp state; always DROP ... IF EXISTS at start AND end
- Never use FORCE INDEX — add covering indexes and let the optimizer choose
- Never use dynamic SQL / CONCAT of user input into SQL strings

### Java
- Java 25 — use records, sealed classes, pattern matching, text blocks, virtual threads
- No Spring, no Quarkus, no Guice — zero framework dependencies in boxy-core/boxy-mysql
- All DB access via repository classes extending BaseRepository — no inline JDBC elsewhere
- Records for all domain objects in boxy.core.domain — immutable, no setters
- Catch SQLException, wrap in DataAccessException (unchecked) — never swallow exceptions
- Use SLF4J for logging; always include entity IDs and operation names in log messages
- No string concatenation to build JSON — use a JSON library

### Liquibase
- Never edit an existing changeset — add a new one instead (changesets are immutable once applied)
- Use <sqlFile> with splitStatements="false" and endDelimiter="//"
- One changeset per stored procedure drop-and-recreate

### Testing
- Extend BaseIT for all integration tests (Testcontainers MySQL 8.0.43)
- Use TestData.seed(dataSource) in @BeforeEach for standard fixtures
- No Thread.sleep() — use Awaitility or polling with timeout
- Name tests: <method>_<scenario>_<expectedOutcome>

---

## Critical Anti-Patterns — Never Do This

- ❌ Add Thread.sleep() in tests
- ❌ Add Spring / Quarkus / other framework dependencies to boxy-core
- ❌ Add FORCE INDEX hints to new SQL
- ❌ Edit existing Liquibase changesets
- ❌ Build JSON with string concatenation
- ❌ Push directly to main or refactor (always use a feature branch + PR)
- ❌ Write SQL outside of *Repository classes
- ❌ Commit broken tests
- ❌ Make performance changes without benchmark evidence

---

## Module Layout

```
boxy/
├── boxy-db/          # Liquibase migrations + all SQL
│   └── db/changelog/mysql/
│       ├── sp/       # Stored procedures: sp_<entity>__<action>.sql
│       ├── fn/       # Functions: fn_<name>.sql
│       └── events/   # MySQL scheduled events
├── boxy-core/        # Java domain records, repository implementations
│   └── boxy/core/
│       ├── domain/   # Immutable Java records
│       ├── mapper/   # RowMapper implementations
│       ├── repository/ # JDBC repositories (extends BaseRepository)
│       ├── DataSourceProvider.java
│       └── DataAccessException.java
├── CLAUDE.md         # AI agent context
├── AGENTS.md         # Agent workflow rules (branch naming, commit format, PR rules)
└── CONTRIBUTING.md   # Human + agent contributor guide
```

---

## Key Domain Concepts

| Term | Meaning |
|------|---------|
| Namespace | Hierarchical path container (closure table). Case-sensitive. |
| Topic | Belongs to a namespace; fixed partition count (1–1024). |
| Partition | Shard of a topic. ID = (topic_id << 16) + partition_number. |
| Event | LONGBLOB payload. Published into events + unprocessed_events; sequenced by background process. |
| Subscription | Named consumer group. Links to topics via subscription_topics. |
| Cursor | Consumption position per (subscription, partition). Has random_key for fair-share distribution. |
| Consumer | Registered client instance. UUID v4 ID. Has heartbeat deadline. |
| Consumer Lease | 3s lock: consumer ↔ cursor during active polling. |

---

## Performance Target

1M events/second sustained throughput on AWS r6g.2xlarge or equivalent with provisioned IOPS MySQL.
All performance changes MUST include before/after benchmark numbers using the BenchmarkIT profile.

---

## Branch Naming

| Contributor | Prefix |
|------------|--------|
| Claude / Claude Code | `codex/` |
| JetBrains Junie | `junie/` |
| Cursor | `cursor/` |
| Human | `feat/`, `fix/`, `chore/`, `docs/` |

---

## Commit Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <description> [item #N]

<why, not what>

Closes: Phase X, item N of PRODUCTION_READINESS.md

Co-Authored-By: <Agent> <noreply@anthropic.com>
```

Types: feat, fix, perf, refactor, test, docs, chore
Scopes: agents, cli, core, mysql, pgsql, db, benchmark, ci

---

## Files That Need Paired Updates

- Stored procedure file + its Liquibase changeset
- Repository method + its mapper + its domain record
- Performance change + docs/benchmarks.md
- User-facing change + README.md
- Any completed item + CHANGELOG.md

---

## Before Starting Any Task

1. Read CLAUDE.md (architecture context)
2. Read AGENTS.md (workflow rules)
3. Check PRODUCTION_READINESS.md (current work items)
4. Check CHANGELOG.md (what's already done)
5. Create a branch: `cursor/<short-description>`
